# Dry-run publish gate phase 6 (TERMINAL): Receipt & Replay — Kestrel
# Toolkit release-candidate case study. One domain FRAGMENT of the shared
# kestrel-dry-run-publish-cycle domain: this phase's 3 actions chain
# cleanroom-complete -> receipt-step1-done -> receipt-step2-done -> dry-run-verified,
# so the merged cycle plan can only reach this phase after Phase 5
# (Clean-Room Verification) completes. 8-constraint split: every
# precondition/effect/goal here is a 1-conjunct (and ...) — far inside
# PDDL8_MAX_CONJUNCTS=8 — and each action takes 1 parameter
# (PDDL8_MAX_PARAMS=8); the dry-run harness asserts these bounds
# mechanically for every fragment (reusing
# crate::bench::togaf::verify_eight_constraint_split verbatim).
#
# DRY-RUN-OVERCLAIM FENCE (this fragment carries the terminal goal atom,
# so read this carefully): the terminal effect atom is named
# "dry-run-verified", deliberately NOT "receipt-complete" and emphatically
# NOT "published", "crates-io-uploaded", or "release-complete" — no such
# atom exists anywhere in this domain. This is the one disclosed exception
# to the pack's uniform "{phase}-complete" naming convention (see
# packs/dry-run-publish-pack/ontology.ttl): the terminal atom must read
# unambiguously as "dry run" because it is also the merged problem's sole
# GOAL atom, and a generic phase-completion word could be misread as
# "release shipped". The third action, confirm-byte-identical-replay-no-mutation,
# reaches dry-run-verified only after recording external_mutation=false;
# the dry-run harness (crates/cng/src/bench/dry_run_publish_test.rs) is
# expected to grep the parsed, merged Pddl8Domain's action effects for
# "published"/"crates-io-uploaded"/"release-complete" and assert zero
# matches, exactly as soc2_test.rs greps for "compliant"/"opinion". This
# fragment is the structural enforcement point for that check, not just
# prose. The terminal deliverable is a DRY-RUN EVIDENCE BUNDLE for a human
# release manager's go/no-go decision, never the decision itself and never
# a claim that a live `cargo publish` (without --dry-run) ran. See
# packs/dry-run-publish-pack/ontology.ttl for the full fence disclosure.
#
# Public-ontology doctrine: the artifact node is a blank node; the phase is
# identified by its public SKOS notation. The only private predicate is
# the cng pipeline's ABI carrier ceng:pddlDomain (urn:chatman:engine#),
# disclosed in packs/dry-run-publish-pack/ontology.ttl.
@prefix ceng:    <urn:chatman:engine#> .
@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

_:artifact
    skos:notation "DRY-RUN-RECEIPT" ;
    dcterms:description "Receipt & Replay (terminal) domain fragment of the kestrel-dry-run-publish-cycle STRIPS domain; the terminal effect atom is dry-run-verified, reached only after external_mutation=false is recorded."@en ;
    ceng:pddlDomain """
(define (domain kestrel-dry-run-publish-cycle)
  (:requirements :strips)
  (:predicates
    (cleanroom-complete ?x)
    (receipt-step1-done ?x)
    (receipt-step2-done ?x)
    (dry-run-verified ?x))
  (:action emit-final-receipt
    :parameters (?x)
    :precondition (and (cleanroom-complete ?x))
    :effect (and (receipt-step1-done ?x)))
  (:action attach-ocel-evidence
    :parameters (?x)
    :precondition (and (receipt-step1-done ?x))
    :effect (and (receipt-step2-done ?x)))
  (:action confirm-byte-identical-replay-no-mutation
    :parameters (?x)
    :precondition (and (receipt-step2-done ?x))
    :effect (and (dry-run-verified ?x))))
""" .
